abstract: >-
  Research drafts and exact verification scripts for the random friend-tree
  growth exponent and a related family of local redirection models. The
  original-model draft develops an exact scalar pressure characterization,
  effective two-sided computation, a uniform boundary-leaf resolvent bound,
  robustness under bounded predictable boundary input, and an improved
  rational upper certificate. The companion draft proves almost-sure growth
  and irrationality of the local-model exponent for finite algebraic
  activation parameters. A third draft gives the exact original-kernel
  first-promotion transform, rational-summation classification, certified
  tail bounds, and sharp coefficient-height asymptotics at algebraic
  discounts. Irrationality and transcendence of the original random
  friend-tree exponent remain open.
